+# 2026-10-25-web-search-switch
+
+English | [中文](2026-10-25-web-search-switch.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+Adds the log-only web/search event that records the per-Session web-search switch state.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Declaration](#declaration)
+- [Compatibility](#compatibility)
+- [Verification](#verification)
+- [Dev Note](#dev-note)
+
+<a id="declaration"></a>
+## Declaration
+
+```yaml persistence-change
+schemaVersion: 1
+id: 2026-10-25-web-search-switch
+baseline: false
+changes:
+  - root: "event:web/search"
+    previous: null
+    after: "5f940e8aa1c0edbc54d323596422ded5c3f8c673df6b8e15a77e1f3a8564ed49"
+    decision: same-version
+```
+
+<a id="compatibility"></a>
+## Compatibility
+
+A new root in the same Session format version. Existing logs contain no such event and fold to enabled, which is the behavior before the event existed, so they stay valid with unchanged meaning. Readers that predate it refuse a log carrying it, as every required-on-read event does. The event is appended only by dsh-tool-web's /web command and its step-start append; the event itself never enters model input, and it decides whether later steps offer web_search, web_fetch, and the prefix-matched tools.
+
+<a id="verification"></a>
+## Verification
+
+pnpm exec vitest run packages/web/tool-web: 138 tests passed in 5 files, including the web-search-switch suite's resumed-log, fork-seed, and cold-replay cases.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+## Dev Note
+
+None.
