+---
+kind: upgrade-guide
+description: MCP Streamable HTTP endpoints that redirect now fail instead of forwarding requests.
+---
+
+# Configure final MCP HTTP endpoints
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+MCP Streamable HTTP refuses redirects, including same-origin redirects. Configured endpoints still receive the initial request, but redirect targets receive neither custom credentials nor request bodies. Deployments that configure a redirecting URL must update it.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. Find each `dsh-mcp-client` entry with `transport: streamable-http` in your profile configuration.
+2. Set `url` to the trusted final MCP endpoint, including the required path and trailing slash. Do not copy an untrusted redirect target.
+3. Restart the profile and confirm the server's tools load. A redirect error means the configured endpoint still redirects; correct the URL or server routing.
