+
+Effort levels always come from the adapter's catalog for the exact model, so each model shows its own number of levels. Where a route advertises a broader generic list, a preset narrows it to the levels the vendor's API accepts, as pi-ai's model data records them (for example Low, Medium, and High for Gemini 4 Argon, or Low, High, and Max for Kimi K3); DeepSeek models keep the levels DeepSeek's own adapter declares. A model that offers both an off level (`off` or `none`) and at least one thinking level shows the "Extended thinking" switch. Its thinking levels appear as pills while it thinks, when it offers two or more of them; a model that always thinks shows the pills without a switch. ← and →, Home, and End change the level, and every change applies at once and keeps the popover open. Turning thinking on applies the catalog default when it thinks, else High, Medium, or the strongest level.
