+
+Ratings, descriptions, first-token waits, and prices come from three layers, highest first. The first is what the user enters in the "Model details in the picker" card on Settings → Models. The second is the prices last read from the public price source models.dev. The third is the built-in presets for well-known models of Anthropic (Claude), OpenAI (GPT), Google (Gemini), Moonshot (Kimi), Alibaba (Qwen), Zhipu (GLM), MiniMax, DeepSeek, and xAI (Grok). Presets match the vendor's model id, known aliases, `vendor/model` route ids, and ids with a trailing release date. The cost rating derives from the output price unless the user sets one. Prices are vendors' list prices in US dollars per million tokens; some vendors price by time of day, for example DeepSeek's peak hours cost double and models.dev records the off-peak price.
