+<a id="icon-motion"></a>
+#### Icon motion
+
+`icon-motion.css` gives product icons motion modeled on [lucide-animated](https://lucide-animated.com) (MIT). An icon plays a short motion while the control around it — a button, link, summary, label, or element with an interactive role, unless disabled — is hovered or keyboard-focused, and returns to its drawing when the control is left; hovering a bare icon works too. Whole-glyph motions turn, wobble, pop, or fly the icon: they key on its `data-icon` and animate its `<svg>` box, so they also move theme-replaced artwork. Part motions are `dsw-motion-*` classes on elements of the default ui-primitives artwork, such as a check that draws itself in or a trash lid that lifts, and reach the sprite symbol through `<use>`. Two inherited variables carry the state: `--dsw-icon-play` names no animation at rest and becomes guaranteed-invalid while active, so `var(--dsw-icon-play, <keyframes>)` falls back to the motion, and `--dsw-icon-on`, 0 or 1, drives the poses held while active. A component starts an icon's motion without hover by setting `--dsw-icon-play: initial` on the icon's `<svg>`. Every rule has zero specificity, so an animation or transform a component sets on an icon wins. Motion needs a hover-capable pointer and no reduced-motion preference; the loader and the tree connector keep still.
