+<a id="web-search-switch"></a>
+### Turning web search off for a session
+
+Type `/web off` to stop offering the model web tools in the current session, and `/web on` to offer them again; a client sends the same line through the commands service. The state belongs to one session, starts on, and is logged as the `web/search` event, so resume and fork keep it. Successful `command/done` records the selected target and immediately governs admission, including between turns. The next accepted pre-step consolidates it into `web/search`; selecting the opposite state before then cancels the change. Results read `Web search off.`, `Turning web search off (applies from the next step).`, `Web search stays on.` after a cancellation, or `Web search is already off.`, with the matching `on` forms; any other argument fails with `Use /web on or /web off.` The web GUI draws no chat row for `/web on` or `/web off`, typed or sent by the model picker's switch, because the picker shows the state; a failed argument keeps its row.
+
+While the switch is off, a step admits neither `web_search` nor `web_fetch`, and the agent also loses every global or preset tool whose name starts with a `webSwitchToolPrefixes` entry. The default list covers common web MCP servers — `mcp__exa__`, `mcp__tavily`, `mcp__brave`, `mcp__perplexity`, `mcp__firecrawl`, `mcp__fetch__`, and `mcp__jina` — so a profile that searches through an MCP server such as Exa loses that path too. Matching tools disappear as soon as `/web off` is selected, so a call to one that the running step has not dispatched yet fails as `UNKNOWN_TOOL`; a matching tool registered later is withheld from the step after the next accepted step start.
+
+Clients read the `webSearch` session projection, `{ enabled, pending }`: `enabled` is the logged state, and `pending` is true while a successfully settled `/web` selection of the other state waits to be logged. Tool admission reads that same successful target after Session reconstruction; unfinished or failed commands preserve the previous selection. Import its type with `import type { WebSearchProjection } from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-web/client'`; host code uses `/types`. The switch is installed when `search` or `fetch` is enabled and activates only where `dsh-session-projection` is composed; `/web` also needs the command and agent registries. Without the projection registry the key is absent and both tools follow readiness alone. The key is registered globally: clients also check that the current agent offers `/web`, because a preset-scoped installation does not make its command available outside that scope.
 
